From 3a9e535023a83e88b04d1400c0481d5cf0b2ea90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:13:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Controls scale with the screen DPI; no pointer during the
 splash

- Layout::scale now follows the screen's logical DPI (1x at 96), so icons,
  switches, sliders, stylesheet padding and dialogs grow with point-sized
  text instead of staying at their pixel size when QT_FONT_DPI is raised.
  Fonts already follow the DPI and are not scaled again. The nav rail's
  Side Bar Scale applies on top. The colour wheel and keyboard keys start
  smaller so their dialogs still fit at about 2x.
- Full-screen dialogs size their body to its content (up to the space the
  window has) instead of the scroll area's small default, which clipped
  the colour pop-up behind a scrollbar.
- With the cursor setting off (or auto-hide on) the pointer is hidden from
  the first frame: EGLFS drew its arrow in the top-left corner during the
  splash, before Dash applied the setting.
